# Runtime Shim SELinux rules.
#
# The Zygisk companion channel hands the app a unix stream socket that was
# created while the process was still in the zygote SELinux domain, so the
# socket object keeps the "zygote" label after the process specializes to
# untrusted_app. Stock policy denies untrusted_app most socket operations on
# zygote-labeled sockets, which surfaces as EACCES(13) on the first send()
# and disables the input channel (passive runtime only).
#
# Grant the app domain exactly the operations the channel uses:
# read/recvfrom (responses), write/sendto (requests), getopt (SO_COOKIE
# validation), setopt/getattr (descriptor hygiene).
allow untrusted_app zygote unix_stream_socket { read write sendto recvfrom getattr getopt setopt }
